# Critique

Read the requested file, or all files in `manuscript/main/` if no file
is given. Do not edit files during the critique and do not invent
citations.

Report the highest-risk issues first:

- unsupported or overstrong claims
- unclear methods
- missing citations or comparisons
- weak results reporting
- reproducibility gaps
- limitations that should be acknowledged

For one section, then add line-level feedback: unclear sentences,
citation problems, broken cross-references, structure and wordiness.

Quote the exact text and give its file. Rewrite only when the user
asks.
